  "semantic_contract": "Connected original flight/environment/lifecycle contracts. BYTEBB9 is FF for normal control but 1 after celestial-body transfer; nonnegative state halves speed/control accumulators and steps rotation0 by6 modulo4096 untilzero, then writesFF. BYTEBBA is cleared by contact collection each frame, receives2 on structure exit or FF/FE on orientation-dependent entry; mouse/player control consumers bypass free flight and force original poses. BYTEBBB enables resuming interruptedgame: gameplay start and successful load set, gameover/viewer/loadstart clear; E3D4 tests it before resuming. Not a pointer-serialization flag. BYTEBB5 is modulo4 divider used solely by nearby Solice update to decrement angle once per4calls, initialized3 on world/newgame. BYTEBB7 is world atmosphere flag: indexed16-byte table37B58 selects FF/0 and eventmessages11/10 say Atmosphere/NoAtmosphere Detected; surface type145 disc overlay also checks it. Unknown higher selector domains and original sideeffects retained. Rotation2 event spin uses signed WORD39CDA (64steps, negativeinactive) and restore WORD39CDC; expiry restores angle and writesFFFF. These static contracts explain original byte states, not new runtime scenarios, universal physical time or all-entry validity.",
